1
00:02:07,915 --> 00:02:17,345
Visit turkision.com for more!

2
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:22,079
So you say you'll
hit us from behind..

3
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:26,759
...if we break the heathens behind you...

4
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:29,759
...and attack Mekece, huh?

5
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:34,279
You're marching to the castle
which is under my protection.

6
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:39,599
Not to let you tell others
that we hit you from behind

7
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:42,839
...we are speaking face to face.

8
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:46,239
If you just go away

9
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:48,919
...no blood will be shed in vain.

10
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:53,999
Don't make us to create battlefield here!

11
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:58,199
The vilest battlefield ever seen, Yakup Bey!

12
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:03,159
You put the heathens forward
and come behind us like snakes!

13
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:06,799
Alright then! Let's start the battle then!

14
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:10,919
Let's see who is the snake and who is the wolf!

15
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:14,679
Only Allah knows who's going to die...

16
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:19,839
...if there is to be a battle here!

17
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:26,319
Kayi may lose the battle. But both Candar...

18
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:32,519
...and Germiyan will lose too many here!

19
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:39,479
Those afraid of losing...

20
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:43,039
...can never reach the victory!

21
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:45,319
This is not the matter..

22
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,119
...today here.

23
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:51,679
If we fight each other,

24
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:54,079
..if we shed blood

25
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:56,359
...then...

26
00:03:56,880 --> 00:03:59,919
...this hostility will never end.

27
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:04,439
Next generations will keep killing each other.

28
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:07,199
No.

29
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:09,599
And then...

30
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:12,519
...no Turkish beylics...

31
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:18,279
...will manage to become a state under one flag.

32
00:04:20,399 --> 00:04:22,639
So, Osman Bey...

33
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:24,999
Will you stop?

34
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,999
Not for you.

35
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,999
I'll stop for my dreams.

36
00:04:56,760 --> 00:04:58,599
For my dreams.

37
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:02,359
Good!

38
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:09,119
Draw your alps back then!

39
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:15,279
Alps!

40
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:23,759
Osman Bey, they're playing a game. Don't you see?

41
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:27,919
Gunduz Bey.

42
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:35,319
Okay. Whatever you say, Osman Bey.

43
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:39,759
If I sense any hostility in Mekece

44
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:41,359
..then...

45
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:44,959
...all of you will be my enemies!

46
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:48,439
Whatever army confronts me

47
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:50,719
...I will never stop!

48
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:52,959
Mekece Castle..

49
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:58,079
...isn't the land of heathens!
It won't be hostile to you!

50
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:00,359
Osman Bey.

51
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:06,639
Let me host you in my new land.

52
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:09,479
-Orhan.
-My Bey.

53
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:13,999
Alaaddin! Gunduz Bey! You
go to the tribe with the alps.

54
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:15,439
I am...

55
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:20,479
...going to Mekece with Beys.

56
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:25,919
I'm going to Mekece...

57
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:29,639
...so I can see what they gave for it.

58
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:30,599
Come on.

59
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:32,959
-As you order, my Bey.
-As you order, my Bey.

60
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:34,719
Okay, Osman Bey.

61
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,279
Come on, Beys!

62
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,479
What's going on?

63
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:52,399
Why are they still not attacking?

64
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:55,879
UIcay, there is no fighting.

65
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:59,119
Osman is coming to the castle.

66
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:02,519
Cowards!

67
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:06,959
If you show your teeth, you have to bite!

68
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:10,279
They'll make a deal. There will be peace.

69
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:12,319
What now?

70
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:14,959
Their deal will be ruined with blood.

71
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:18,319
Peace is only for losers.

72
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:21,599
Only the brave can fight.

73
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:26,319
Osman won't be able to
get out of this castle alive.

74
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:30,919
The castle is still under Ibrahim Bey's protection.

75
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:33,759
When Osman loses his head...

76
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:37,559
...his sons will come for vengeance.

77
00:07:38,760 --> 00:07:42,999
And then the beylics will fight each other.

78
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:54,719
What are we going to do here, my Bey?

79
00:07:55,960 --> 00:08:00,399
We should see Mekece which
is going to be our property, right?

80
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:04,679
We won't stop, huh, my Bey?

81
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:09,159
Even the heathens couldn't stop us.

82
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:12,599
So I won't be stopped by
a few words of them. Well...

83
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:19,039
I set Mekece as my prey.

84
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:26,319
So nobody can stop me.

85
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:44,038
You'll see Cerkutay.

86
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:48,519
They won't keep their promise.

87
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:53,999
They don't intend to stop us only.

88
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:57,439
The ones working with the heathens against us...

89
00:08:57,720 --> 00:09:01,439
...can do anything to wipe us out of these lands.

90
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:13,799
With their first mistake, we'll
take the castle from them.

91
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:18,519
We'll take even their heads.

92
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:22,199
So...

93
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:26,759
You should keep your eyes wide open now.

94
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:29,239
For the conquest of this castle

95
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:32,439
...you should gather all the information, Cerkutay.

96
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:37,359
That's the reason why we've come here.

97
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:39,159
As you order, my Bey.

98
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:41,599
-As you order, my Bey.
-As you order, my Bey.

99
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:47,799
Alps and I will get to know
every corner of our new land-to-be.

100
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:51,119
Absolutely. Come on.

101
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:54,799
Mekece...

102
00:09:57,040 --> 00:09:58,999
Mekece...

103
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:14,119
My sons, are you alright?

104
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:17,159
-We're fine, mother.
-Thanks to Allah, we're fine.

105
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:19,999
Where is Osman Bey?

106
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:24,959
Ibrahim Bey and Yakup Bey
took Mekece under their protection.

107
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:28,519
My father will be their guest.

108
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:36,359
We fell into the nest of the evil.

109
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:40,879
Yet we looked behind and
climbed out of it, Bala Hatun.

110
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:50,479
My father must have a plan, Gunduz Bey.

111
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:58,479
Yes. Osman Bey must have a good plan.

112
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:02,199
Of course, your father has a plan.

113
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:06,879
But I know the hearts of those people!

114
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:12,799
You don't take my words seriously, though.

115
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:20,039
-Gunduz Bey.
-Alaeddin.

116
00:11:23,400 --> 00:11:24,359
Gunduz Bey.

117
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,799
Let us talk the rest at somewhere else.

118
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:34,759
Come on.

119
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:39,279
What happened happened.
There is not much else to talk!

120
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:44,239
Allah, grant me patience.

121
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:47,119
What happened to you? Are you alright?

122
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:49,719
I am alright, my rose.

123
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:53,159
My Shahzade, come on.

124
00:11:57,920 --> 00:11:58,959
Ghazi.

125
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:01,759
I am heading out to duty.

126
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:05,479
Look after my Hatun well.

127
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:07,839
Alright?

128
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:10,479
Do not worry, my Shahzade.

129
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:15,279
I can even guard her tent, for sure.

130
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:18,199
Praise be to my valiant.

131
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:21,119
Come on then.

132
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:25,559
Come on.

133
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:32,679
This Gunduz Bey got grumpy like my mother.

134
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:34,999
You can not say that!

135
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:39,599
Did you call your mother grumpy?

136
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:42,559
I only say the truth!

137
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:46,559
I saw it! I saw him blowing off his steam!

138
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:51,359
What will I do with this one, Gonca?

139
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:52,959
I don't know, Ulgen.

140
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:57,719
You heard the Shahzade.

141
00:12:57,720 --> 00:13:01,719
Gonca Hatun is entrusted to me.
Do not come close, Ulgen Hatun!

142
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:04,439
Look at this one.

143
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:07,359
Don't act mad! Or you will get the slap.

144
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:09,119
Here.

145
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:13,079
You are grumpy!

146
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:14,959
Grumpy!

147
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:41,719
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

148
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:46,759
So, Osman Bey.

149
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:51,279
For whom it is intended
and for whom it is destined.

150
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:57,799
Conquering Mekece Castle
was written in our destiny.

151
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:02,999
May Allah..

152
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:07,639
..allow you to rule it..

153
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:10,719
..with righteously, Ibrahim Bey.

154
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:16,679
If you make a mistake..

155
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:20,599
..you will not hold this place for long, alright?

156
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:26,519
Do not worry about those issues, Osman Bey.

157
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:30,759
Because of the peace that was granted..

158
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:35,159
..Mekece will be one of our most wealthy cities.

159
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:41,559
The trade that goes from west to east..

160
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:45,359
..will start from this castle.

161
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:49,999
Lord?

162
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:54,319
If Osman Bey wants to benefit from this trade..

163
00:14:54,320 --> 00:14:57,079
..he will need your approval.

164
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:05,959
There is always a stubborn stone..

165
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:09,999
..that stops a flowing river.

166
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:11,479
At worst..

167
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:15,159
..it makes it change the route.

168
00:15:17,040 --> 00:15:22,159
Is your intention to be a
stone on our road, Osman Bey?

169
00:15:23,920 --> 00:15:25,079
Let us know.

170
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:31,039
Only time and your acts will determine that.

171
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:35,319
Ibrahim Bey.

172
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:51,199
Let us wander around..

173
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:55,279
..Mekece now.

174
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:06,999
Soon..

175
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:11,399
..Lords of Iznik and Bursa..

176
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:14,559
..will join our trade.

177
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:23,039
Then, the Frontier Marketplace...

178
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:26,039
...will leave its name for
"Grand Marketplace" if Allah permits.

179
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:31,399
We will handle the trade..

180
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:33,919
..in both west and east.

181
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:40,319
We rather be small..

182
00:16:41,320 --> 00:16:44,559
..than to trade with infidels..

183
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:50,439
..and grow in these lands.

184
00:16:56,920 --> 00:16:57,839
However..

185
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:02,559
..I do not want to intervene in your business.

186
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:08,358
-..if something happens to the
people- -You can not intervene anyways.

187
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:19,519
Because, we've calculated everything..

188
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:23,358
..and did what is needed.

189
00:17:24,119 --> 00:17:27,959
You will either stay with us..

190
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:30,959
..or against us.

191
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:35,799
As you big brothers..

192
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:40,039
..we want to give you a piece of our powers.

193
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:59,639
You are trying to work with infidels.

194
00:17:59,640 --> 00:18:03,439
And you are trying to
make us fall for that as well.

195
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:09,679
I will never fall for that.

196
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:20,719
You got us wrong, Osman Bey.

197
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:26,279
The days when we wanted to
see you with us, were left behind.

198
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:31,399
From now on..

199
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:36,119
..you can only be behind us.

200
00:18:36,120 --> 00:18:41,759
And that can only happen with full loyalty.

201
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:54,479
Loyalty you say.

202
00:18:56,320 --> 00:19:00,079
Loyalty is only provided to a ruler.

203
00:19:03,040 --> 00:19:08,799
You have no rule over us.

204
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:27,199
Our loyalty is only for our cause.

205
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:46,479
Catch that dog.

206
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:10,839
Osman Bey.

207
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:17,079
You should've let us fight
until the last drop of our blood.

208
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:20,879
The tricks are big, Gunduz
Bey. They've united with infidels.

209
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:21,959
Yes.

210
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:27,279
Now, we need to spill their bloods as well.

211
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:34,879
We should've defeated that
Germiyanid and that Candar.

212
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:39,439
Gunduz Bey. Of course, we
will not fall back from fighting.

213
00:20:39,440 --> 00:20:42,199
We will repay them a thousand more.

214
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:45,719
If I know my father, he thinks like this as well.

215
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:50,399
You father let this team of dastards walk.

216
00:20:51,440 --> 00:20:53,639
Look at our situation here.

217
00:20:53,640 --> 00:20:57,679
Kayis do not fall from the field of battle!

218
00:20:57,680 --> 00:21:01,359
They do not, Gunduz Bey.

219
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:04,719
We never ran away from any fight.

220
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:08,319
However, we always avoided
spilling the blood of our brothers.

221
00:21:08,320 --> 00:21:10,719
-My father- -Alaeddin!

222
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:19,079
One you avoided spilling
blood of is working with infidels.

223
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:25,959
Are you refraining because
Germiyan is your father-in-law?

224
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:28,719
Gunduz Bey.

225
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,759
I do not discriminate.

226
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:35,399
I never discriminate just
because of father-in-law, know that.

227
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:40,959
Bala Hatun.

228
00:21:41,720 --> 00:21:45,999
I am going to my tribe. Let Osman Bey know.

229
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,919
Come on. Stay well.

230
00:22:00,640 --> 00:22:02,679
You are still answering to Gunduz Bey..

231
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:08,959
..instead of keeping it calm, Alaeddin.

232
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:12,999
Don't you hear what he is saying, brother?

233
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:17,879
I had to answer. He blamed
me for protecting Yakup Bey.

234
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:23,799
I've heard what Gunduz Bey said, Alaeddin.

235
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:30,839
However, I've heard what you
said to Gunduz Bey before as well.

236
00:22:30,840 --> 00:22:34,199
You know the reason why
Gunduz Bey is so angry, right?

237
00:22:35,680 --> 00:22:41,079
You scolded a Bey of tribe in front of alps.

238
00:22:41,680 --> 00:22:42,919
Sons.

239
00:22:43,440 --> 00:22:45,759
Stay calm.

240
00:22:47,560 --> 00:22:48,519
Alaeddin.

241
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:51,119
You brother is right.

242
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:55,919
Gunduz Bey is very angry
about what happened lately.

243
00:22:56,360 --> 00:22:59,799
Staying against him in a
time like this will not do.

244
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:01,879
You need to make peace with him at once.

245
00:23:03,720 --> 00:23:04,479
Alright.

246
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:11,559
We will send the goods to Bursa tomorrow.

247
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:14,919
-At a time like this?
-This is my father's command.

248
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:18,479
We will go to Ulcay's den with Alaeddin.

249
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:21,159
It is time to make that dog talk.

250
00:23:21,160 --> 00:23:24,919
My father, is making plans to take that castle.

251
00:23:25,640 --> 00:23:28,919
-However, Gunduz Bey is not aware of this.
-Yes.

252
00:23:30,320 --> 00:23:35,999
My Bey was not pleased about
Gunduz Bey's impulsive outburst.

253
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:38,239
So that's why he was angry.

254
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:40,119
Alright.

255
00:23:42,240 --> 00:23:45,119
It seems we will have a new castle tomorrow, right?

256
00:23:45,120 --> 00:23:47,879
We will, if Allah permits, mother.

257
00:23:47,880 --> 00:23:49,999
If Allah permits.

258
00:24:20,400 --> 00:24:25,199
You're doing something wrong in the wrong castle.

259
00:24:28,120 --> 00:24:32,719
We know what the Alps who
brought Ahmet Bey's body said.

260
00:24:32,720 --> 00:24:36,799
The killer used the dagger with his right hand.

261
00:24:36,800 --> 00:24:41,879
If he hadn't been angry, using the
dagger would have been enough...

262
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:43,279
...but it wasn't.

263
00:24:43,760 --> 00:24:48,999
He grabbed his throat with his left hand
and used the dagger with his right hand.

264
00:24:50,200 --> 00:24:54,719
The killer will show his anger again, Osman Bey.

265
00:24:54,720 --> 00:24:56,639
What is this situation?

266
00:24:56,920 --> 00:25:00,839
Osman Bey is our guest in this castle!

267
00:25:00,840 --> 00:25:04,039
Tugay! How did you let this happen?

268
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:13,199
That was the ruling I was
talking about, Ibrahim Bey.

269
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:15,359
You talk about ruling...

270
00:25:15,880 --> 00:25:19,639
...but they are challenging you here.

271
00:25:24,280 --> 00:25:25,239
Mehmet.

272
00:25:26,280 --> 00:25:28,599
Do not kill this dog.

273
00:25:29,600 --> 00:25:36,319
What was his purpose by attempting
to kill Osman Bey in our property?

274
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:40,719
I will learn all this by pulling
those words out of his mouth!

275
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:41,839
Alps!

276
00:25:45,280 --> 00:25:50,719
Your eyes will be on all
the soldiers in the castle!

277
00:25:51,160 --> 00:25:54,439
If there is such an attack again...

278
00:25:56,720 --> 00:25:59,719
...you will pay for it, Tugay!

279
00:26:01,400 --> 00:26:02,719
Osman Bey!

280
00:26:04,080 --> 00:26:08,199
All my soldiers are under
the command of our laws...

281
00:26:08,200 --> 00:26:09,919
...know that.

282
00:26:09,920 --> 00:26:14,599
Don't try using this attack.

283
00:26:14,600 --> 00:26:20,639
After what I did today, I
hope Osman Bey forgives me.

284
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:28,279
Your soldiers are loyal to the laws.

285
00:26:29,440 --> 00:26:31,039
But we'll see...

286
00:26:31,600 --> 00:26:32,999
..if you are...

287
00:26:35,360 --> 00:26:37,999
...loyal to the laws...

288
00:26:40,480 --> 00:26:42,999
...or not.

289
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:48,199
We'll see.

290
00:26:52,880 --> 00:26:55,559
The words we say..

291
00:26:55,560 --> 00:26:58,359
...are now the laws, Osman Bey.

292
00:27:00,040 --> 00:27:00,879
Come on.

293
00:27:01,760 --> 00:27:03,119
Let's go inside.

294
00:27:04,080 --> 00:27:05,559
Let's go.

295
00:27:07,360 --> 00:27:09,359
Yakup Bey.

296
00:27:17,440 --> 00:27:20,039
I will go and make that dog speak.

297
00:27:29,120 --> 00:27:30,479
Continue?

298
00:27:31,200 --> 00:27:33,199
Continue what, Cerkutay?

299
00:27:33,200 --> 00:27:36,679
Will you continue walking on the wrong path?

300
00:27:37,360 --> 00:27:39,959
Your way is the only right way, right?

301
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:41,319
No.

302
00:27:43,160 --> 00:27:45,839
The way is the way of truth, it is not our way.

303
00:27:45,840 --> 00:27:51,399
But... at least we are not
protecting the castle of infidels.

304
00:27:53,280 --> 00:27:57,039
We are conquering castles
without shedding blood, Cerkutay.

305
00:27:57,680 --> 00:28:00,199
Cerkutay... Good.

306
00:28:02,560 --> 00:28:06,239
We conquered many lands, brother.

307
00:28:07,440 --> 00:28:09,399
This conquest...

308
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:11,919
...this..

309
00:28:13,280 --> 00:28:16,519
...this is preventing the fire of gaza.

310
00:28:23,280 --> 00:28:27,119
If Crusaders are wandering around the yard...

311
00:28:27,680 --> 00:28:29,919
...I cannot call that place our homeland.

312
00:28:31,480 --> 00:28:32,759
Now..

313
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:38,239
...listen to your conscience...

314
00:28:38,240 --> 00:28:40,239
...and see the truth.

315
00:28:41,040 --> 00:28:42,199
Or else...

316
00:28:43,800 --> 00:28:47,319
...this move will hurt you the most.

317
00:29:07,840 --> 00:29:11,319
Look at my Bala..

318
00:29:11,320 --> 00:29:14,119
She already prepared the dowery, huh?

319
00:29:15,760 --> 00:29:21,119
My mother started preparing the dowry before
my brother was able to confess his love.

320
00:29:21,120 --> 00:29:22,319
Right!

321
00:29:22,800 --> 00:29:26,439
But he used to say he was not in love then...

322
00:29:26,440 --> 00:29:29,559
But now we are preparing their dowry, huh?

323
00:29:32,520 --> 00:29:34,799
This was not necessary, Bala Hatun.

324
00:29:35,880 --> 00:29:38,159
Why, my daughter?

325
00:29:38,160 --> 00:29:41,039
It is not even enough for my children.

326
00:30:00,040 --> 00:30:02,159
Gonca...

327
00:30:04,120 --> 00:30:06,439
Come... Come.

328
00:30:13,960 --> 00:30:14,919
My daughter...

329
00:30:16,720 --> 00:30:21,119
You sacrificed great things for this love.

330
00:30:21,120 --> 00:30:25,719
There is a fire in your heart that
gets stronger every time a wind blows.

331
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:26,599
I can see it.

332
00:30:28,280 --> 00:30:30,439
Can't I put this fire out?

333
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:37,719
I... was used to my mother and brother.

334
00:30:39,760 --> 00:30:41,399
But my father..

335
00:30:44,960 --> 00:30:46,439
I... used to...

336
00:30:46,520 --> 00:30:52,239
...run away from everything and
everyone and take shelter in him.

337
00:30:52,920 --> 00:30:55,719
Now I feel like a bird that fell out of its nest.

338
00:30:58,880 --> 00:31:00,159
No, my daughter...

339
00:31:02,400 --> 00:31:05,119
I know... I know, my daughter.

340
00:31:07,600 --> 00:31:08,799
But...

341
00:31:09,640 --> 00:31:12,359
...that bird did not fall off its nest.

342
00:31:12,360 --> 00:31:16,519
She left its nest to build its own nest.

343
00:31:20,280 --> 00:31:21,719
And now...

344
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:27,839
...she will build her own nest,
she will be stronger than before.

345
00:31:28,840 --> 00:31:32,759
You won't be alone when
you are starting your family.

346
00:31:33,160 --> 00:31:35,879
I will always be with you, my daughter.

347
00:31:37,720 --> 00:31:39,559
You were always with me.

348
00:31:41,240 --> 00:31:43,999
My mother was not with me...

349
00:31:44,600 --> 00:31:46,959
...but you were.

350
00:31:51,400 --> 00:31:53,919
Now if you allow me...

351
00:31:54,400 --> 00:31:56,559
...I want to call you "mother".

352
00:32:03,400 --> 00:32:08,239
Does anyone ever ask for permission
to call their mother "mother"?

353
00:32:10,760 --> 00:32:11,999
Yes.

354
00:32:12,680 --> 00:32:13,919
Yes..

355
00:32:23,240 --> 00:32:24,799
My beautiful daughter...

356
00:32:33,960 --> 00:32:38,919
I'm grateful... I'm grateful
you're Aladdin's mother.

357
00:32:40,360 --> 00:32:43,119
Thankfully, you are our mother.

358
00:32:45,640 --> 00:32:47,679
Bala mother..

359
00:32:50,680 --> 00:32:53,439
Say that again.

360
00:32:54,640 --> 00:32:56,959
Bala mother...

361
00:33:17,520 --> 00:33:20,039
You understood me, right?

362
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:24,559
Tonight, you will put this in
Gonca and Alaeddin's room.

363
00:33:24,560 --> 00:33:30,879
Every breath they take will bring
them closer to death step by step.

364
00:33:41,760 --> 00:33:44,079
Why is that Hatun here again?

365
00:33:45,200 --> 00:33:48,399
It's obvious that she's not
here for something good.

366
00:33:53,640 --> 00:33:57,719
Cerkutay, I want all the information about Mekece.

367
00:33:57,720 --> 00:34:01,319
Where are the enters and exits
and how many soldiers are there?

368
00:34:01,320 --> 00:34:05,239
Where they put the archers.
Inform me about all of this.

369
00:34:05,240 --> 00:34:10,158
Yes, my Bey. We'll start
the duty when the night falls.

370
00:34:11,480 --> 00:34:12,518
But, my Bey.

371
00:34:13,239 --> 00:34:15,319
Sorry for my curiosity.

372
00:34:15,600 --> 00:34:20,079
We sent all the alps to the
tribe, it seems we won't besiege.

373
00:34:20,080 --> 00:34:20,759
My Bey.

374
00:34:21,360 --> 00:34:23,239
What's on your mind?

375
00:34:25,360 --> 00:34:28,039
We'll see who is the soldier and who is not.

376
00:34:29,120 --> 00:34:31,399
We will hunt them down.

377
00:34:31,400 --> 00:34:34,319
Now they smile at us.

378
00:34:34,679 --> 00:34:38,039
But I know that this is not the truth.

379
00:34:43,600 --> 00:34:48,559
Even if they find out that Alaeddin is
innocent, Ibrahim Bey and Yakup Bey

380
00:34:49,639 --> 00:34:52,359
will definitely cause a problem.

381
00:34:53,480 --> 00:34:56,518
Anger has blinded them, my Bey.

382
00:34:57,200 --> 00:35:02,239
One for his dead son and one
for his daughter who ran away.

383
00:35:03,640 --> 00:35:07,999
The truth will slap them in the face.

384
00:35:08,920 --> 00:35:13,519
Mekece will be our land with Allah's permission.

385
00:35:14,160 --> 00:35:16,919
-If Allah permits, my Bey.
-If Allah permits, my Bey.

386
00:35:16,920 --> 00:35:18,239
If Allah permits, my Bey.

387
00:36:01,600 --> 00:36:03,719
-Konur Bey.
-My Shahzade.

388
00:36:04,160 --> 00:36:05,839
-My Shahzade?
-Boran Bey.

389
00:36:08,600 --> 00:36:11,399
My Shahzade.

390
00:36:16,160 --> 00:36:18,999
Praise be! Praise be!

391
00:36:20,040 --> 00:36:22,839
Osman Bey, Cerkutay, are they alright?

392
00:36:22,840 --> 00:36:25,439
-Thankfully, they are alright.
-They are alright.

393
00:36:25,440 --> 00:36:29,919
Ibrahim and Yakup Bey did not
trust us enough to come close to them.

394
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:34,719
When I found out about their
Mekece move, it was too late.

395
00:36:35,560 --> 00:36:39,399
But they will pay for this treachery.

396
00:36:39,400 --> 00:36:42,119
Let us get rid of the doubts.

397
00:36:42,120 --> 00:36:45,719
Their doubts will be gone
and they will trust you more.

398
00:36:45,720 --> 00:36:50,519
When you capture Ulcay, they will fall
for the trap and trust you so much that

399
00:36:50,520 --> 00:36:53,879
from now on they will want
to do everything with you.

400
00:36:53,880 --> 00:36:55,559
I hope so.

401
00:36:57,400 --> 00:37:00,199
Children, listen to me very carefully.

402
00:37:00,200 --> 00:37:04,719
We will not kneel to them nor
we will leave the castle to them.

403
00:37:04,720 --> 00:37:06,319
-Alaeddin.
-My Bey.

404
00:37:07,200 --> 00:37:11,399
Take Gonca and Holofira and take goods to Bursa.

405
00:37:12,080 --> 00:37:15,999
Your route will be the borders of Mekece.

406
00:37:16,840 --> 00:37:18,439
Yes, my Bey.

407
00:37:19,400 --> 00:37:24,239
Yakup and Ibrahim Bey
won't like it and try to stop it.

408
00:37:24,240 --> 00:37:28,959
They will send support units from
the castle and stop the caravan.

409
00:37:30,200 --> 00:37:32,399
That's my sons.

410
00:37:34,080 --> 00:37:36,319
That's exactly what's going to happen.

411
00:37:36,760 --> 00:37:42,119
So that the castle will be empty
and the conquest will be easier.

412
00:37:44,560 --> 00:37:45,999
-Orhan.
-My Bey.

413
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:48,514
You will tie the rope
around that jackal named

414
00:37:48,526 --> 00:37:50,999
Ulcay's neck and you'll
take him to the tribe.

415
00:37:52,440 --> 00:37:53,439
Boran

416
00:37:55,160 --> 00:37:56,639
And Konur.

417
00:37:56,800 --> 00:38:00,319
Gather information from them and attack his den.

418
00:38:00,320 --> 00:38:03,307
It is time to find out
who's he collaborating with.

419
00:38:03,319 --> 00:38:04,319
Yes, my Bey.

420
00:38:08,400 --> 00:38:09,199
My Bey.

421
00:38:10,360 --> 00:38:12,399
What about Gunduz Bey?

422
00:38:12,600 --> 00:38:14,999
He's obviously offended.

423
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:23,239
It's not right for a Bey to act
so reckless in the battlefield.

424
00:38:24,360 --> 00:38:28,799
Especially if he's my child's father-in-law.

425
00:38:28,800 --> 00:38:32,199
-Let him rest in the tribe for a while.
-Okay, my Bey.

426
00:38:32,200 --> 00:38:33,239
Come on.

427
00:38:36,840 --> 00:38:38,639
Their dens...

428
00:38:39,120 --> 00:38:41,959
...will become their grave.

429
00:38:41,960 --> 00:38:45,039
-I hope so, my Shahzade.
-Come on.

430
00:39:01,720 --> 00:39:04,559
Won't you say welcome?

431
00:39:06,400 --> 00:39:07,839
Bala Hatun?

432
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:13,719
You haven't been very pleasant since the
day you came to the frontiers, Melike Hatun.

433
00:39:18,200 --> 00:39:20,199
This time I'm here for something well.

434
00:39:21,360 --> 00:39:25,999
Haven't you heard yet? Mekece has become our land.

435
00:39:26,000 --> 00:39:27,599
We're neighbours.

436
00:39:27,600 --> 00:39:29,239
Right, we've heard it.

437
00:39:29,760 --> 00:39:32,239
We've also heard how you took it.

438
00:39:32,800 --> 00:39:34,879
I hope you're not offended.

439
00:39:41,320 --> 00:39:42,279
Anyway.

440
00:39:43,600 --> 00:39:50,559
Since Ibrahim Bey and Yakup Bey talked to Osman
Bey and agreed on it, the hostility is over.

441
00:39:51,240 --> 00:39:53,119
The hostility is over.

442
00:39:53,120 --> 00:39:56,279
You also found the killer of your child Ahmed.

443
00:39:58,160 --> 00:40:01,799
Then what do you want from us, Melike Hatun?

444
00:40:03,640 --> 00:40:05,919
Are we going to talk about it here?

445
00:40:08,400 --> 00:40:13,599
Should I teach you how to host a guest?

446
00:40:18,240 --> 00:40:20,239
Come on, get inside.

447
00:40:40,960 --> 00:40:43,159
Go to hell.

448
00:41:36,160 --> 00:41:39,039
There's a raid!

449
00:42:05,880 --> 00:42:10,199
-Allah is the Greatest!
-Allah is the Greatest!

450
00:43:13,120 --> 00:43:15,119
Allah is the Greatest!

451
00:43:40,960 --> 00:43:44,999
Konur, what are you doing with these guys?

452
00:43:49,160 --> 00:43:51,599
You betrayed Ibrahim Bey.

453
00:43:51,600 --> 00:43:54,439
I've never been in the same path with Ibrahim Bey.

454
00:43:56,200 --> 00:43:59,319
How can one be with these jackals?

455
00:43:59,320 --> 00:44:01,839
It's not clear who's holding their leashes.

456
00:44:01,840 --> 00:44:05,719
They are jackals, but...

457
00:44:06,680 --> 00:44:08,759
...they are loyal.

458
00:44:09,080 --> 00:44:10,799
They are honorable.

459
00:44:11,840 --> 00:44:15,239
They don't laugh in your face
and do things behind your back.

460
00:44:15,280 --> 00:44:19,279
They are letting whoever wants to
shed blood in this land pull the strings.

461
00:44:19,280 --> 00:44:23,319
Husrev. Walking in the same path with these
dastards is deviating from the path of Haqq

462
00:44:23,320 --> 00:44:24,599
-Konur!
-Husrev.

463
00:44:26,160 --> 00:44:27,959
Konur Bey is right.

464
00:44:28,680 --> 00:44:34,159
They killed Shahzade Ahmed
dishonorably to cause a war.

465
00:44:37,120 --> 00:44:38,239
Now.

466
00:44:39,120 --> 00:44:41,599
Now, you'll make a decision here.

467
00:44:41,800 --> 00:44:43,879
Either you'll die

468
00:44:45,800 --> 00:44:48,839
and rot here with them.

469
00:44:49,640 --> 00:44:54,639
Or you will fight by our side in the path
of Haqq against the dishonorable ones.

470
00:46:07,560 --> 00:46:09,439
Osman Bey.

471
00:46:18,440 --> 00:46:23,639
Let me accompany you to dinner.

472
00:46:34,760 --> 00:46:37,599
You did a big job..

473
00:46:38,200 --> 00:46:40,519
..by finding Ahmed's killer.

474
00:46:40,840 --> 00:46:43,439
I only did my duty.

475
00:46:43,440 --> 00:46:45,679
Your son..

476
00:46:45,680 --> 00:46:48,119
..has been found innocent as well.

477
00:46:48,120 --> 00:46:51,159
My son was not guilty to begin with.

478
00:46:52,760 --> 00:46:54,599
We need to know whoever..

479
00:46:54,600 --> 00:46:58,479
..is trying to put us against each other.

480
00:46:59,760 --> 00:47:05,279
Ask those questions to Ibrahim Bey and Yakup Bey.

481
00:47:05,560 --> 00:47:09,119
I only follow orders.

482
00:47:09,120 --> 00:47:11,759
That is the real issue.

483
00:47:11,760 --> 00:47:14,279
Whose orders are you following?

484
00:47:14,280 --> 00:47:16,279
We will see that.

485
00:47:16,440 --> 00:47:21,199
I both saved your life and your son's

486
00:47:23,320 --> 00:47:26,399
You are still acting like an enemy to me.

487
00:47:27,800 --> 00:47:30,439
You need to be my equal first..

488
00:47:30,760 --> 00:47:33,519
..to be my enemy.

489
00:47:34,080 --> 00:47:38,559
Are you my equal to be my enemy?

490
00:47:40,800 --> 00:47:45,439
Now, whoever attacked Ahmed..

491
00:47:47,200 --> 00:47:49,599
..attacked the judge as well.

492
00:47:51,760 --> 00:47:54,079
I am not like others you know.

493
00:47:54,840 --> 00:47:57,519
I know the truth well.

494
00:47:57,520 --> 00:48:01,799
When truth is revealed..

495
00:48:02,800 --> 00:48:05,359
..then I will declare my sentence.

496
00:48:17,080 --> 00:48:21,079
Let us kill Osman while he is here.

497
00:48:22,240 --> 00:48:24,199
Who can stand against us?

498
00:48:24,200 --> 00:48:26,799
Orhan or Alaeddin?

499
00:48:27,480 --> 00:48:30,719
Who can stand against Candarlis and Germiyanids?

500
00:48:32,560 --> 00:48:34,879
You are right, my Mehmed.

501
00:48:35,480 --> 00:48:37,639
No one can stand.

502
00:48:37,640 --> 00:48:42,919
However, we need to think this through.

503
00:48:42,920 --> 00:48:46,199
We will make such plans..

504
00:48:46,200 --> 00:48:51,159
..that leaderless Kayi will follow us.

505
00:48:52,440 --> 00:48:59,519
Commander of Bursa and
castle lords are on their way.

506
00:49:00,200 --> 00:49:02,079
They are coming here.

507
00:49:02,080 --> 00:49:07,839
We will gather all forces in our hands.

508
00:49:10,600 --> 00:49:15,119
Tomorrow, you will go to greet them.

509
00:49:16,040 --> 00:49:20,599
Both power, and trade.

510
00:49:20,880 --> 00:49:23,479
Osman will get stuck in a corner.

511
00:49:23,480 --> 00:49:26,679
He will get stuck so much that..

512
00:49:26,680 --> 00:49:32,359
.he will not have any other
option to bow down to us.

513
00:49:34,760 --> 00:49:37,079
I will bring them here.

514
00:49:40,960 --> 00:49:47,479
Yakup Bey, let us go to Gunduz Bey's tribe as well.

515
00:49:48,240 --> 00:49:52,359
I already sent words to alps.

516
00:49:52,880 --> 00:49:58,079
Let us get into Gunduz Bey's head so much..

517
00:49:58,680 --> 00:50:05,479
..that he will fall to wherever we want.

518
00:50:08,800 --> 00:50:14,319
Your mind is something else, Ibrahim Bey.

519
00:50:14,320 --> 00:50:16,319
Thank you.

520
00:50:25,160 --> 00:50:28,199
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

521
00:50:28,200 --> 00:50:31,079
Peace be upon you too.

522
00:50:31,440 --> 00:50:32,719
Here, please.

523
00:50:38,880 --> 00:50:40,839
Beys, what is this?

524
00:50:42,640 --> 00:50:48,799
Did you stray away from your traditions?

525
00:50:51,640 --> 00:50:54,239
Did you forget to sit on the floor?

526
00:50:54,560 --> 00:50:56,199
What is this table?

527
00:51:00,560 --> 00:51:05,599
We do not learn traditions from you.

528
00:51:05,600 --> 00:51:08,679
We are not bound to this table as well.

529
00:51:08,680 --> 00:51:10,919
We have work to do.

530
00:51:11,080 --> 00:51:13,039
Sit down.

531
00:51:17,880 --> 00:51:23,239
New things, Osman Bey.

532
00:51:25,840 --> 00:51:29,879
You will get used to it as well. Come on, sit.

533
00:51:31,040 --> 00:51:34,239
Authority does not corrupt anyone.

534
00:51:35,440 --> 00:51:41,079
It only reveals what a person
is really inside, Ibrahim Bey.

535
00:51:42,960 --> 00:51:47,159
It seems, this is who you really are.

536
00:51:51,440 --> 00:51:55,399
By working with this infidel..

537
00:51:55,400 --> 00:51:58,999
..you got used to their traditions.

538
00:52:28,640 --> 00:52:31,679
-Brother?
-Tell me, Alaeddin.

539
00:52:35,720 --> 00:52:38,239
So you are still mad at me.

540
00:52:43,920 --> 00:52:46,159
You think so.

541
00:52:50,680 --> 00:52:52,519
Sorry.

542
00:52:53,240 --> 00:52:58,159
I., you know.. I can't keep my mouth shut.

543
00:53:04,760 --> 00:53:09,919
You are not the only one,
Alaeddin. Fatma is like you as well.

544
00:53:09,920 --> 00:53:14,119
-It seems I am being tested with you.
-Don't say that.

545
00:53:14,120 --> 00:53:16,239
Am I that bad, brother?

546
00:53:16,240 --> 00:53:19,799
No one can hold you back.

547
00:53:19,800 --> 00:53:22,799
You have to say the truth boldly.

548
00:53:25,560 --> 00:53:29,319
I said the wrong thing, with the burden of duty.

549
00:53:30,120 --> 00:53:33,359
I didn't think Gunduz Bey would be offended.

550
00:53:37,040 --> 00:53:40,119
I know, Alaeddin.

551
00:53:41,440 --> 00:53:44,119
What Gunduz Bey did was wrong.

552
00:53:44,120 --> 00:53:45,719
However, manners.

553
00:53:46,000 --> 00:53:49,599
Manners is of great importance to us, Alaeddin.

554
00:53:49,600 --> 00:53:54,199
Do not think that I am protecting Gunduz Bey.

555
00:53:54,200 --> 00:53:57,239
I would've said the same
thing if it was another Bey.

556
00:53:57,240 --> 00:53:59,559
Especially in a war time like this.

557
00:53:59,560 --> 00:54:02,879
We need to not offend the Beys that are with us.

558
00:54:05,040 --> 00:54:07,759
You are right, brother.

559
00:54:10,960 --> 00:54:16,079
After my duty is done, I will
make peace with Gunduz Bey.

560
00:54:19,160 --> 00:54:21,319
You forgive me as well, alright?

561
00:54:26,480 --> 00:54:31,079
-My brother.
-Thanks to Allah, brother. Thanks to Allah.

562
00:54:34,640 --> 00:54:36,519
Well, Boran Bey.

563
00:54:36,880 --> 00:54:39,839
Like old times, huh? Come on.

564
00:54:40,080 --> 00:54:42,159
Start playing kopuz.

565
00:54:44,280 --> 00:54:45,919
Alright, my Shahzade.

566
00:54:46,160 --> 00:54:49,679
Here we go. Well...

567
00:54:50,800 --> 00:54:53,039
Well...

568
00:57:40,360 --> 00:57:42,239
Praise be!

569
00:57:42,320 --> 00:57:45,199
Well sung, Boran Bey!

570
00:57:45,200 --> 00:57:47,639
You excited us about fighting!

571
00:57:47,760 --> 00:57:49,639
Thank you, my Shahzade.

572
00:58:00,480 --> 00:58:03,879
Let's talk about the matter.

573
00:58:04,560 --> 00:58:07,519
It's not a good time to be stubborn.

574
00:58:08,040 --> 00:58:11,999
Our land has gone through hard times.

575
00:58:12,680 --> 00:58:17,399
Now we have a great chance.

576
00:58:18,440 --> 00:58:24,319
The trade route to be opened from
east to west will be under our control.

577
00:58:26,880 --> 00:58:32,439
People will be at ease as
long as peace is provided.

578
00:58:32,920 --> 00:58:36,319
Great Beys are speaking so well.

579
00:58:37,920 --> 00:58:41,319
But they don't speak of the rest.

580
00:58:42,960 --> 00:58:46,119
You tell us then.

581
00:58:46,280 --> 00:58:48,919
So we can know, Osman Bey.

582
00:58:48,920 --> 00:58:52,799
Our trade from east to west...

583
00:58:54,880 --> 00:58:57,159
Tell me what the east is.

584
00:59:00,600 --> 00:59:02,639
Olcaytu.

585
00:59:06,360 --> 00:59:10,759
The Ilkhanid State. They
caused Great Seljuks to collapse.

586
00:59:10,880 --> 00:59:14,999
They destroyed our tribes and killed our children.

587
00:59:16,360 --> 00:59:17,639
Well...

588
00:59:18,080 --> 00:59:21,679
So you want to grow bigger...

589
00:59:22,080 --> 00:59:24,919
...by trading with them, huh?

590
00:59:27,160 --> 00:59:29,079
And what about the west?

591
00:59:29,360 --> 00:59:32,919
Byzantine attempted to...

592
00:59:33,640 --> 00:59:37,599
...send an army of Crusaders to
our lands just a few months ago.

593
00:59:38,520 --> 00:59:40,959
They killed our children.

594
00:59:42,760 --> 00:59:50,039
We should have no peace and no deals with them.

595
00:59:51,480 --> 00:59:56,999
It seems you want to let
the heathens have the bridle.

596
00:59:57,040 --> 00:59:59,759
Nobody can bridle us, Osman Bey.

597
00:59:59,880 --> 01:00:01,599
Don't be worrying.

598
01:00:03,840 --> 01:00:08,359
What you're saying is all the past, Osman Bey.

599
01:00:08,480 --> 01:00:13,279
What is past is past.

600
01:00:14,840 --> 01:00:20,519
Don't be one of those who look
behind but can't see forward, Osman Bey.

601
01:00:20,800 --> 01:00:25,959
Either be with us or be nothing.

602
01:00:26,800 --> 01:00:29,719
We won't let you trade.

603
01:00:29,760 --> 01:00:32,399
Do whatever you can!

604
01:00:39,440 --> 01:00:42,439
The move you're trying to make...

605
01:00:42,480 --> 01:00:46,919
...will let the dying Byzantine rise again.

606
01:00:47,440 --> 01:00:53,759
It'll give a chance to Olcaytu who is
looking for a chance to jump on us!

607
01:00:56,920 --> 01:00:58,479
No.

608
01:00:59,160 --> 01:01:02,479
I will never give you
permission to do this to my land.

609
01:01:02,480 --> 01:01:06,839
Nobody needs your permission, Osman.

610
01:01:07,120 --> 01:01:10,359
We did what we did.

611
01:01:11,160 --> 01:01:13,679
It's your turn to decide.

612
01:01:13,880 --> 01:01:18,439
If you pledge loyalty and obey us,

613
01:01:19,880 --> 01:01:24,359
...you will prosper with us.

614
01:01:25,680 --> 01:01:27,839
If you don't

615
01:01:28,920 --> 01:01:31,719
...you will vanish.

616
01:01:38,880 --> 01:01:41,479
We have two ways ahead of us.

617
01:01:43,680 --> 01:01:45,999
But either of the ways..

618
01:01:47,160 --> 01:01:49,359
...will destroy us.

619
01:01:52,720 --> 01:01:54,879
The right to do is...

620
01:01:56,200 --> 01:01:58,959
...standing against you.

621
01:02:02,240 --> 01:02:05,759
I will let nobody have an easy victory.

622
01:02:06,600 --> 01:02:09,279
Then, Osman Bey...

623
01:02:09,880 --> 01:02:12,679
Your fate is determined.

624
01:02:13,000 --> 01:02:16,119
It's me who will determine your fates.

625
01:02:20,840 --> 01:02:25,559
Like you determined Boran's and Konur's fates?

626
01:02:25,720 --> 01:02:28,879
Those men fought behind you for years.

627
01:02:28,960 --> 01:02:32,279
You can't even make your own men listen to you.

628
01:02:32,320 --> 01:02:35,919
But you are showing off to Beys here.

629
01:02:37,480 --> 01:02:39,999
Look at that jackal.

630
01:02:41,880 --> 01:02:43,759
Look at that jackal.

631
01:02:44,280 --> 01:02:47,879
He thinks he can speak freely here.

632
01:02:53,280 --> 01:02:55,759
I will treat my land..

633
01:02:57,120 --> 01:03:00,359
...just as I treat my soldiers.

634
01:03:00,960 --> 01:03:04,919
If someone makes a mistake,

635
01:03:06,080 --> 01:03:12,159
...I will mind no other
things and just cut him off!

636
01:03:19,480 --> 01:03:23,279
They made a mistake and now are paying for it.

637
01:03:24,880 --> 01:03:26,719
Just wait.

638
01:03:28,080 --> 01:03:29,599
Just wait.

639
01:03:29,920 --> 01:03:33,959
You will pay for what you did as well.

640
01:03:34,080 --> 01:03:38,679
You will make me pay, Osman Bey?

641
01:03:39,640 --> 01:03:44,079
Your justice can't harm my skin.

642
01:03:44,400 --> 01:03:48,719
I'm not one of your people.

643
01:03:50,560 --> 01:03:54,959
Justice is only for us.

644
01:03:56,160 --> 01:03:58,959
And for you

645
01:03:59,680 --> 01:04:02,399
...there is only a sharp sword.

646
01:04:04,480 --> 01:04:06,119
You'll see.

647
01:04:07,320 --> 01:04:08,999
You will see.

648
01:04:09,320 --> 01:04:11,759
You're waiting for your time.

649
01:04:12,920 --> 01:04:16,079
Osman Bey, pull yourself together.

650
01:04:16,280 --> 01:04:20,759
You're threatening my soldiers in front of me!

651
01:04:21,040 --> 01:04:25,759
He's not threatening only
me but also you, Ibrahim Bey!

652
01:04:28,120 --> 01:04:29,799
Ulcay!

653
01:04:30,560 --> 01:04:32,479
Get out.

654
01:04:57,160 --> 01:05:00,159
What is your final decision, Osman Bey?

655
01:05:02,400 --> 01:05:06,719
If you accept, we will become
much stronger together, Osman Bey.

656
01:05:07,280 --> 01:05:10,679
The fight never stops but just waits for its time.

657
01:05:11,080 --> 01:05:13,119
Stand behind my father.

658
01:05:13,440 --> 01:05:15,239
And be stronger.

659
01:05:18,960 --> 01:05:20,959
Thank you, boys.

660
01:05:23,320 --> 01:05:24,559
Thank you.

661
01:05:26,680 --> 01:05:30,959
Obviously, you fathers
will never walk in this way...

662
01:05:31,480 --> 01:05:34,199
...even if they see the truth.

663
01:05:36,680 --> 01:05:39,279
But you will see.

664
01:05:40,400 --> 01:05:45,879
Soon, you'll see the poison under the cruel.

665
01:05:49,400 --> 01:05:51,799
The battle does not wait for anything.

666
01:05:52,800 --> 01:05:55,679
Have a blessed night.

667
01:06:00,680 --> 01:06:04,079
It will be your last peaceful night.

668
01:06:21,360 --> 01:06:28,679
This night, the battle will
definitely begin with Osman's death.

669
01:06:30,760 --> 01:06:33,479
His children will attack

670
01:06:33,480 --> 01:06:38,879
Germiyan and Candaroglus for revenge.

671
01:06:38,880 --> 01:06:41,479
You made him attack Osman.

672
01:06:41,960 --> 01:06:46,679
You gained their trust and caused
suspicion in bashibozouk soldiers.

673
01:06:47,560 --> 01:06:51,079
This night

674
01:06:52,440 --> 01:06:57,479
you will take Osman to me silently.

675
01:07:05,640 --> 01:07:08,959
I'll send Osman's head

676
01:07:08,960 --> 01:07:11,999
to Olcaytu.

677
01:07:18,360 --> 01:07:22,959
So, long story short,

678
01:07:23,920 --> 01:07:26,399
I forgive you, Gonca.

679
01:07:26,840 --> 01:07:28,039
Is that so?

680
01:07:29,800 --> 01:07:33,879
We didn't do anything that you should forgive.

681
01:07:35,080 --> 01:07:37,639
I forgive you too, Holofira.

682
01:07:38,640 --> 01:07:41,719
We don't have any reason to seek forgiveness.

683
01:07:41,720 --> 01:07:44,799
You do, but

684
01:07:46,240 --> 01:07:48,879
but since you're naive, I won't dwell on it.

685
01:07:51,160 --> 01:07:52,799
Anyway

686
01:07:53,280 --> 01:07:57,159
We will unite against all of
the enemies in these lands.

687
01:07:57,160 --> 01:07:59,879
Right. That's right, but

688
01:08:00,480 --> 01:08:02,599
I'm a bit confused.

689
01:08:03,800 --> 01:08:06,799
Who's the enemy, Melike Hatun?

690
01:08:09,400 --> 01:08:12,119
You united with the Lords.

691
01:08:17,479 --> 01:08:22,999
While you have Holofira on your
table are you asking for an enemy?

692
01:08:24,040 --> 01:08:27,398
Isn't Holofira Byzantine?

693
01:08:28,479 --> 01:08:30,479
Right, Holofira?

694
01:08:32,279 --> 01:08:36,799
So not all the Byzantines are enemies.

695
01:08:36,800 --> 01:08:41,238
Those we can get along with
are friends, the others are enemies.

696
01:08:41,240 --> 01:08:44,919
Holofira is a daughter of
this household, Melike Hatun.

697
01:08:45,600 --> 01:08:47,799
She's our daughter.

698
01:08:49,200 --> 01:08:53,879
Since we're friends from now on...

699
01:08:53,880 --> 01:08:59,599
...then we need to find the
traitor who tried to kill my child...

700
01:08:59,600 --> 01:09:04,639
and who killed Rukneddin The Judge
and replaced him with a fake judge.

701
01:09:05,960 --> 01:09:07,318
Of course.

702
01:09:08,000 --> 01:09:09,078
Of course.

703
01:09:09,880 --> 01:09:14,679
We're also very curious
about who did this treachery.

704
01:09:17,359 --> 01:09:18,719
Who's that?

705
01:09:20,160 --> 01:09:24,519
Who wanted to kill Alaeddin?

706
01:09:24,840 --> 01:09:28,038
It must be someone who doesn't trust justice.

707
01:09:28,040 --> 01:09:32,919
Someone who knew judge
would find Alaeddin innocent.

708
01:09:37,240 --> 01:09:40,318
Right. You're right.

709
01:09:40,680 --> 01:09:44,318
Maybe that Byzantine infidel who killed my son

710
01:09:44,319 --> 01:09:48,318
and shed his blood did this treachery

711
01:09:48,319 --> 01:09:52,599
We cannot know where the
treachery come from, Melike Hatun.

712
01:09:52,600 --> 01:09:57,199
How could a Byzantinian know your judge...

713
01:09:57,200 --> 01:10:00,919
...that replace him with the fake one.

714
01:10:03,840 --> 01:10:05,159
Isn't that right?

715
01:10:11,360 --> 01:10:12,479
Right.

716
01:10:15,680 --> 01:10:16,959
That's true.

717
01:10:23,960 --> 01:10:28,999
If Allah permits,
we will sing our folk songs in Bursa.

718
01:10:29,000 --> 01:10:32,799
If Allah permits, if Allah permits.

719
01:10:33,760 --> 01:10:40,919
When Allah give us the chance, your crown
will drop even if you're the king in Bursa.

720
01:10:41,520 --> 01:10:43,399
We will succeed, if Allah permits.

721
01:10:44,240 --> 01:10:48,959
-We will turn my father's dreams into reality.
-If Allah permits, my brother.

722
01:11:20,720 --> 01:11:21,919
Orhan Bey.

723
01:11:23,560 --> 01:11:24,919
Alaeddin Bey.

724
01:11:27,520 --> 01:11:31,599
I knew that you and Osman
Bey were on the right path.

725
01:11:31,600 --> 01:11:34,759
But I'm sure now.

726
01:11:36,800 --> 01:11:38,159
Tell me

727
01:11:39,080 --> 01:11:41,879
I'm ready to do anything for you.

728
01:11:48,440 --> 01:11:52,119
Thank you, Husrev. Thank you.

729
01:11:54,440 --> 01:11:55,999
Then...

730
01:11:56,480 --> 01:12:00,319
...you'll do a very important duty for us.

731
01:12:00,320 --> 01:12:03,879
Just name it. What's that duty?

732
01:12:12,040 --> 01:12:13,599
You'll be...

733
01:12:16,000 --> 01:12:19,719
...our key to Mekece.

734
01:12:55,480 --> 01:12:58,679
What smells in here?

735
01:13:10,360 --> 01:13:12,239
What kind of smell is this?

736
01:15:57,800 --> 01:16:03,399
Let's see what will you do when
you don't have a sword to use.

737
01:16:18,880 --> 01:16:22,919
What are you doing here at this hour, kiddo?

738
01:16:28,680 --> 01:16:30,319
Who am I talking to?

739
01:16:36,040 --> 01:16:38,799
What are you doing here...

740
01:16:44,120 --> 01:16:46,159
Stop, wait!

741
01:16:46,200 --> 01:16:47,639
What are you doing?

742
01:16:48,440 --> 01:16:53,519
Don't you know what will happen to you if
you cut my Osman Bey's right-hand man.

743
01:16:55,000 --> 01:16:58,279
Cerkutay Bey. Cerkutay.

744
01:17:03,120 --> 01:17:05,759
Where am I? What's this place?

745
01:17:05,760 --> 01:17:09,039
Cerkutay Bey, you were sleepwalking again.

746
01:17:09,040 --> 01:17:12,559
This jackal would have killed
you if I hadn't gotten there.

747
01:17:16,640 --> 01:17:19,279
Was he going to kill me?

748
01:17:19,960 --> 01:17:25,599
It suits him to kill a man without a sword.

749
01:17:25,840 --> 01:17:28,319
He's a jackal after all.

750
01:17:30,480 --> 01:17:33,279
Don't get in my way.

751
01:17:34,080 --> 01:17:38,199
Or I'll crush you
both like a rat.

752
01:17:38,640 --> 01:17:41,159
Get out of here.

753
01:17:41,160 --> 01:17:45,399
I wish you hadn't woken me, Aykurt.

754
01:17:45,400 --> 01:17:48,599
I would have killed him in my sleep.

755
01:17:48,600 --> 01:17:50,599
Look at me.

756
01:17:51,520 --> 01:17:54,399
I don't have customs.

757
01:17:54,840 --> 01:17:57,599
I don't have a rule.

758
01:17:58,360 --> 01:18:03,479
I don't care that you're a
guest and I'll kill you both here.

759
01:18:04,120 --> 01:18:08,199
Get out of here.

760
01:18:15,160 --> 01:18:18,999
Our swords will meet soon.

761
01:18:19,000 --> 01:18:22,039
Be patient.

762
01:18:23,640 --> 01:18:26,639
Aykurt, let's go.

763
01:20:28,840 --> 01:20:33,519
I haven't seen her since I came,
where's your other daughter-in-law Bala?

764
01:20:33,520 --> 01:20:38,879
Elcim daughter is in Yenisehir, she has a duty.

765
01:20:40,160 --> 01:20:43,399
She wouldn't want to be here, of course.

766
01:20:49,560 --> 01:20:50,999
Come on then.

767
01:20:52,720 --> 01:20:55,999
Be our guest tonight, Melike Hatun.

768
01:20:57,800 --> 01:21:00,439
Hatuns prepared your tent.

769
01:21:00,440 --> 01:21:02,919
Thank you, my beautiful daughter.

770
01:21:07,960 --> 01:21:10,039
Beys are doing politics.

771
01:21:10,040 --> 01:21:14,119
They cannot think with compassion
and mercy. It's their nature.

772
01:21:14,120 --> 01:21:17,479
But from now on, we, Turkmen women...

773
01:21:17,480 --> 01:21:21,199
...won't allow brotherly blood to be shed, huh?

774
01:21:21,480 --> 01:21:23,679
I hope so, Melike Hatun.

775
01:21:23,680 --> 01:21:27,719
That's been the intention of
us, the Kayi tribe since the past.

776
01:21:34,080 --> 01:21:37,119
I am sorry, my Gonca daughter.

777
01:21:38,040 --> 01:21:41,599
Holofira. I was in pain, I
expect you to forgive me.

778
01:21:43,440 --> 01:21:48,239
When someone loses her
child, she also loses her mind.

779
01:21:50,280 --> 01:21:53,999
Good night. -Good night.

780
01:22:00,240 --> 01:22:01,799
Mother..

781
01:22:02,240 --> 01:22:05,039
Do you really believe this woman?

782
01:22:06,680 --> 01:22:10,479
Only Allah knows if her intention is good.

783
01:22:10,480 --> 01:22:13,439
We will still be careful, my daughter.

784
01:22:13,440 --> 01:22:15,999
You will also be on alert.

785
01:22:27,880 --> 01:22:29,319
Ertolga!

786
01:22:30,880 --> 01:22:35,119
Go to Yakup Bey and Ibrahim Bey.

787
01:22:35,640 --> 01:22:38,519
Our door will always be open.

788
01:22:38,520 --> 01:22:42,119
They can come. -Yes, Gunduz Bey.

789
01:23:04,760 --> 01:23:08,799
The conqueror of many castles...

790
01:23:09,560 --> 01:23:13,199
...the killer of many brave Byzantium soldiers...

791
01:23:14,400 --> 01:23:16,119
...Osman Bey...

792
01:23:16,480 --> 01:23:19,359
...is now a harmless puppy.

793
01:23:23,280 --> 01:23:25,279
Are you ready, my soldiers?

794
01:23:25,280 --> 01:23:30,519
Today, we will witness the
destruction of a Turkish legend!

795
01:23:33,000 --> 01:23:35,279
The strongest man among the Turks...

796
01:23:35,280 --> 01:23:41,199
...history will write that he
died with my sword today.

797
01:23:42,240 --> 01:23:46,559
Even if your head is needed
by others, I will take your life.

798
01:23:46,840 --> 01:23:49,279
You will die by my sword, Osman!

799
01:23:54,640 --> 01:23:56,159
You dog!

800
01:24:03,080 --> 01:24:08,239
Are you going to kill me, huh? You won't
even be able to see Mekece's conquest!

801
01:24:16,160 --> 01:24:19,759
Not protection, conquest!

802
01:24:24,080 --> 01:24:29,119
Cerkutay! If you hadn't noticed the poison,
we would have been in a difficult position.

803
01:24:29,880 --> 01:24:33,799
Since I track the scent of food, my
nose has a good sense of smell my Bey.

804
01:24:33,800 --> 01:24:37,879
I have also caught the scent
of these dogs' trap, for sure.

805
01:24:41,800 --> 01:24:42,919
Ahmed...

806
01:24:43,840 --> 01:24:44,959
Ahmed...

807
01:24:46,720 --> 01:24:47,879
My son...

808
01:25:02,040 --> 01:25:03,599
Ahmed...

809
01:25:05,440 --> 01:25:06,919
My son.

810
01:25:07,440 --> 01:25:10,239
Wake up, my son...

811
01:25:11,200 --> 01:25:12,439
Stand up..

812
01:25:12,560 --> 01:25:14,319
Come on, wake up.

813
01:25:21,840 --> 01:25:22,879
Mother...

814
01:25:26,360 --> 01:25:28,319
Kill my killer, mother.

815
01:25:29,160 --> 01:25:30,999
Where is Ahmed?

816
01:25:31,440 --> 01:25:33,159
What did you do to my son?

817
01:25:33,640 --> 01:25:35,599
Kill my killer.

818
01:25:35,600 --> 01:25:40,999
Where is my son? Where is Ahmed? Where is my son?

819
01:25:42,040 --> 01:25:44,279
Kill my killer, mother.

820
01:25:45,160 --> 01:25:48,719
It's because of you... You were the reason!

821
01:25:49,960 --> 01:25:52,079
It's because of you!

822
01:25:52,080 --> 01:25:58,919
It's because of you!
It's because of you!

823
01:25:59,640 --> 01:26:03,919
It's because of you!

824
01:26:05,640 --> 01:26:07,799
Ahmed! Ahmed!

825
01:26:25,680 --> 01:26:27,839
What do Kayis want, Andra?

826
01:26:27,840 --> 01:26:29,959
Holofira and Gonca Hatun..

827
01:26:29,960 --> 01:26:33,879
They will take the goods to
Bursa and Iznik to do business.

828
01:26:34,640 --> 01:26:36,719
They are getting ready.

829
01:26:43,080 --> 01:26:47,079
Ibrahim Bey showed his
foresight by sending us here.

830
01:26:47,080 --> 01:26:52,079
And we will do as he ordered and watch their steps.

831
01:26:52,960 --> 01:26:57,959
Now... we have to prevent this business.

832
01:26:59,040 --> 01:27:02,319
Go and inform Ibrahim Bey now.

833
01:27:02,920 --> 01:27:03,799
Stop!

834
01:27:05,360 --> 01:27:07,999
Don't tell him that Gonca will go there as well.

835
01:27:08,000 --> 01:27:11,199
Yakup Bey should not stop
him because of his daughter.

836
01:27:15,440 --> 01:27:18,959
My son is under the soil because of them.

837
01:27:19,680 --> 01:27:25,119
And I will do my best until
I bring the end of Kayis.

838
01:27:25,120 --> 01:27:26,719
I swear..

839
01:27:27,440 --> 01:27:31,519
Did you get all the information
regarding the conquest of the castle?

840
01:27:32,280 --> 01:27:35,319
I have all of them my Bey. Here.

841
01:27:35,320 --> 01:27:36,799
Thank you.

842
01:27:37,560 --> 01:27:39,479
Mekece, huh?

843
01:27:40,160 --> 01:27:41,919
Mekece...

844
01:27:50,640 --> 01:27:53,039
Damn it.

845
01:27:53,840 --> 01:27:57,719
You could not die, Osman. You are still alive!

846
01:28:01,480 --> 01:28:05,519
Here... Before tomorrow night...

847
01:28:05,520 --> 01:28:07,999
..this place will be ours if Allah permits.

848
01:28:08,000 --> 01:28:10,319
-If Allah permits, my Bey.
-If Allah permits, my Bey.

849
01:28:10,320 --> 01:28:11,719
If Allah permits, my Bey.

850
01:28:14,200 --> 01:28:16,239
Mekece...

851
01:28:52,640 --> 01:28:54,759
Lord Matheus!

852
01:28:58,040 --> 01:29:01,319
He is hanged in the courtyard of his own property.

853
01:29:07,280 --> 01:29:09,639
What did you do, Osman?

854
01:29:11,720 --> 01:29:13,999
Who was he allied with?

855
01:29:15,240 --> 01:29:18,239
Why did you kill the Lord?!

856
01:29:20,040 --> 01:29:25,199
He had poison put into the lantern in my room.

857
01:29:25,880 --> 01:29:27,799
He asked me to come.

858
01:29:28,040 --> 01:29:30,759
He tried to kill me!

859
01:29:33,400 --> 01:29:35,519
And I killed him.

860
01:29:35,520 --> 01:29:37,519
Now tell me.

861
01:29:37,960 --> 01:29:41,199
Which one of you were
holding the leash of this dog?

862
01:29:48,560 --> 01:29:51,879
We didn't know about this!

863
01:29:51,880 --> 01:29:54,399
Apparently, he
did this on his own.

864
01:29:54,411 --> 01:29:56,239
If you worked with him...

865
01:29:56,240 --> 01:30:00,079
...then I will see you as infidels, know that!

866
01:30:00,080 --> 01:30:04,839
But if you tell me that you fell into
heedlessness and that's why you let him...

867
01:30:04,840 --> 01:30:10,119
...then the one who falls into
heedlessness can never stand by our side!

868
01:30:13,800 --> 01:30:16,679
That dog's blood watered this soil.

869
01:30:16,680 --> 01:30:19,999
Now this place is about to be our homeland.

870
01:30:20,760 --> 01:30:23,919
You know...

871
01:30:24,640 --> 01:30:27,559
In times of war, peace is never made!

872
01:30:28,160 --> 01:30:34,519
Your own fist is better than a stranger's food.

873
01:30:39,480 --> 01:30:45,639
I will make you learn this by force if necessary.

874
01:30:47,920 --> 01:30:52,199
This is not a place of friends anymore.
This is not the land of Turks anymore!

875
01:30:52,320 --> 01:30:55,519
With Allah's permission, I will..

876
01:30:55,840 --> 01:30:59,719
..make this place Turks' land.

877
01:30:59,920 --> 01:31:03,879
-Pull yourself together Osman!
-You pull yourself together!

878
01:31:04,200 --> 01:31:08,999
I will make you learn. Come
on, this is not the time to talk.

879
01:31:09,240 --> 01:31:13,599
Are you declaring war on us, Osman?

880
01:31:16,880 --> 01:31:20,999
Come on, Osman. Start that war already.

881
01:31:32,800 --> 01:31:37,039
"So do not take them as allies.."

882
01:31:37,240 --> 01:31:40,319
"..unless they emigrate in the cause of Allah."

883
01:31:41,600 --> 01:31:45,359
...Then seize them.."

884
01:31:45,680 --> 01:31:50,279
"..and kill them wherever you find them.

885
01:31:51,160 --> 01:31:56,199
"Do not befriend them.."

886
01:31:56,920 --> 01:32:00,959
"..nor get help from them."
[4:89]

887
01:32:15,840 --> 01:32:18,999
We act on the command of Qur-an.

888
01:32:19,280 --> 01:32:22,639
This place will be conquered for real again!

889
01:32:22,920 --> 01:32:25,359
Let this be known.

890
01:32:39,680 --> 01:32:45,279
Now, Osman will cause chaos.

891
01:33:06,480 --> 01:33:08,879
Osman...

892
01:33:09,480 --> 01:33:13,879
..is sending goods to Bursa with a caravan.

893
01:33:14,560 --> 01:33:17,719
So he will both declare war on us..

894
01:33:18,440 --> 01:33:23,679
..and make business with Bursa at the same time.

895
01:33:23,920 --> 01:33:29,479
No. I will never allow this.

896
01:33:30,760 --> 01:33:32,519
Ulcay!

897
01:33:35,320 --> 01:33:37,679
First..

898
01:33:38,360 --> 01:33:42,759
..send men after the caravan
that is heading to Bursa.

899
01:33:43,000 --> 01:33:47,359
Then, take Konur and Boran with you.

900
01:33:47,480 --> 01:33:51,599
They know Yenisehir the best.

901
01:33:52,320 --> 01:33:55,679
You know what to do.

902
01:33:56,640 --> 01:34:00,279
I will make Yenisehir worse
than Karacahisar Marketplace.

903
01:34:01,080 --> 01:34:05,039
Caravan's road is close to us.

904
01:34:07,560 --> 01:34:10,999
There will a good ambush.

905
01:34:11,160 --> 01:34:13,839
Come on.

906
01:34:16,720 --> 01:34:20,119
Yakup Bey.

907
01:34:21,440 --> 01:34:25,479
I say, we diminish Osman..

908
01:34:25,880 --> 01:34:29,279
..before he prepares the field of battle.

909
01:34:30,320 --> 01:34:32,719
You are right.

910
01:34:32,880 --> 01:34:37,599
Let us go and make peace with Gunduz Bey.

911
01:34:38,080 --> 01:34:41,119
Let them diminish..

912
01:34:41,560 --> 01:34:45,079
..and let us grow.

913
01:34:46,160 --> 01:34:50,239
Let us see what will Gunduz Bey say.

914
01:34:51,600 --> 01:34:56,159
Take that lord down.

915
01:35:02,680 --> 01:35:06,279
-We couldn't talk, Gonca.
-Everything happened so fast..

916
01:35:06,560 --> 01:35:09,039
..I feel like it was a dream, Holofira.

917
01:35:09,160 --> 01:35:12,279
I hope the nightmare part of your life is over.

918
01:35:12,520 --> 01:35:15,399
It will be like a good dream to you now.

919
01:35:15,480 --> 01:35:19,479
I hope so. However, I pray for both of us.

920
01:35:19,680 --> 01:35:22,599
I want you to be good as well.

921
01:35:24,760 --> 01:35:27,399
They are coming.

922
01:35:31,920 --> 01:35:34,069
Halt.

923
01:35:36,800 --> 01:35:41,999
It is forbidden for Kayi caravan to enter Bursa.

924
01:35:43,240 --> 01:35:47,879
With which permission? I am
Princess Holofira, open the road.

925
01:35:48,280 --> 01:35:53,079
Princess, what kind of Roman are
you, travelling with these barbarians?

926
01:35:53,160 --> 01:35:55,639
-Have you no shame?
-Watch your words, commander!

927
01:35:55,720 --> 01:35:58,919
-I have nothing to be ashamed of. -Princess.

928
01:35:59,000 --> 01:36:02,279
-This is my last warning.
-Or what?

929
01:36:02,360 --> 01:36:06,199
Or I will kill all of you without hesitation.

930
01:36:13,560 --> 01:36:19,079
Turks do not fear! We do not give up!

931
01:36:19,280 --> 01:36:23,159
We will see who dies and who lives!

932
01:36:23,480 --> 01:36:25,239
Come on, alps!

933
01:36:25,480 --> 01:36:29,759
-Allah is the greatest!
-Attack!

934
01:36:37,160 --> 01:36:40,479
Come here!

935
01:37:33,480 --> 01:37:35,919
-I've come my Gonca.
-Don't worry.

936
01:37:36,000 --> 01:37:38,399
-I've waited for you to come.
-Really now?

937
01:37:38,640 --> 01:37:40,959
Come on then.

938
01:37:44,160 --> 01:37:46,599
It is time to hunt.

939
01:37:47,240 --> 01:37:52,439
We will make a move and stop Osman's trade.

940
01:37:52,720 --> 01:37:56,999
-Finally.
-And how will we do that?

941
01:37:57,960 --> 01:38:04,079
We will attack Yenisehir.

942
01:38:06,200 --> 01:38:10,519
Come on, let us gather some men.

943
01:38:14,040 --> 01:38:18,079
Come on!

944
01:38:43,080 --> 01:38:48,039
The day Ahmed died, you were after us.

945
01:38:50,760 --> 01:38:54,519
You will talk now.

946
01:38:54,720 --> 01:38:56,999
Get up.

947
01:38:57,200 --> 01:38:59,919
Alaeddin!

948
01:39:00,320 --> 01:39:02,839
Alps, get back!

949
01:39:20,600 --> 01:39:23,999
-Are you alright?
-I am alright.

950
01:39:24,160 --> 01:39:30,519
My Gonca, we will go to the
castle. You go back to the tribe.

951
01:39:32,720 --> 01:39:35,359
My Gonca.

952
01:39:35,480 --> 01:39:38,079
The day we feared so much has come, Alaeddin.

953
01:39:38,160 --> 01:39:41,879
The war has started. Now, my father on one side..

954
01:39:41,960 --> 01:39:44,359
..and we are on the other.

955
01:39:46,120 --> 01:39:48,919
I know your worry.

956
01:39:49,600 --> 01:39:52,599
I am on the road to clash with your brother.

957
01:39:54,400 --> 01:39:56,679
However, I know.

958
01:39:57,520 --> 01:40:00,759
Yakup Bey will see the truth.

959
01:40:00,920 --> 01:40:05,199
What if he does not? Then
what will we do, Alaeddin?

960
01:40:17,880 --> 01:40:20,199
Come on alps!

961
01:40:31,840 --> 01:40:36,079
Gonca, are you alright?

962
01:40:38,160 --> 01:40:41,479
This is such a war, Holofira.

963
01:40:41,600 --> 01:40:45,719
My father and brother on one side..

964
01:40:46,480 --> 01:40:50,519
..and the man I love, my heart on the other.

965
01:40:52,840 --> 01:40:56,759
No matter who wins this war..

966
01:40:57,120 --> 01:41:00,559
..I will get hurt.

967
01:41:04,280 --> 01:41:07,519
Come on.

968
01:41:23,400 --> 01:41:27,119
-Peace be upon you
-Peace be upon you, Gunduz Bey.

969
01:41:27,200 --> 01:41:31,399
Peace be upon you too. Welcome.

970
01:41:32,520 --> 01:41:37,559
Gunduz Bey, you must be wondering...

971
01:41:37,960 --> 01:41:41,199
...why we are here.

972
01:41:42,400 --> 01:41:46,359
We wanted Osman Bey to be our guest.

973
01:41:47,120 --> 01:41:51,639
But he declared war against us.
Is that appropriate, Gunduz Bey?

974
01:41:53,480 --> 01:41:56,519
And you want me...

975
01:41:56,640 --> 01:41:59,799
..to choose a side in this war, huh?

976
01:42:02,880 --> 01:42:05,679
Whoever takes no sides...

977
01:42:10,040 --> 01:42:13,239
...will be removed aside, Gunduz Bey.

978
01:42:14,560 --> 01:42:17,559
If you don't want to lose

979
01:42:18,320 --> 01:42:21,279
...you have to choose.

980
01:42:46,960 --> 01:42:49,319
The wolf has raided...

981
01:42:53,880 --> 01:42:56,879
...the nest of the jackal, Ulcay.

982
01:42:57,480 --> 01:43:02,359
-Orhan...
Yes, Orhan.

983
01:43:04,040 --> 01:43:10,639
You will pay a heavy price, though.

984
01:43:11,800 --> 01:43:15,239
We will see.

985
01:43:34,000 --> 01:43:37,599
-You don't care about your life.
-Whose dog are you?

986
01:43:37,840 --> 01:43:40,759
I swear I will make wolves eat you.

987
01:43:41,000 --> 01:43:44,079
You jackal!

988
01:43:48,440 --> 01:43:52,439
-It's like you're attacking heathens, Konur Bey.
-You say so?

989
01:44:14,400 --> 01:44:17,719
Old man, I need you alive.

990
01:44:17,880 --> 01:44:19,719
I have things to do with you.

991
01:44:19,720 --> 01:44:23,319
I swear I will catch you.

992
01:44:28,640 --> 01:44:32,239
Ulcay, you can't run off!

993
01:44:35,200 --> 01:44:39,839
Just run, Ulcay. Let's see how far you can go.

994
01:44:52,880 --> 01:44:55,359
Osman.

995
01:45:08,120 --> 01:45:12,839
Ibrahim Bey will make you pay
a heavy price for this, Osman.

996
01:45:12,840 --> 01:45:14,519
Shut up!

997
01:45:15,320 --> 01:45:18,439
You think you're still Ibrahim Bey's man?

998
01:45:18,520 --> 01:45:23,799
I killed Lord. You took
Ibrahim Bey's soldiers captive.

999
01:45:24,160 --> 01:45:28,559
If you don't let me go,
there will be a war to come.

1000
01:45:29,240 --> 01:45:33,959
We've never been afraid of war! Ever!

1001
01:45:35,240 --> 01:45:38,719
But just be patient. When Ibrahim Bey finds out...

1002
01:45:38,920 --> 01:45:41,479
...who is holding your leash

1003
01:45:41,640 --> 01:45:44,679
...he will want to kill you personally.

1004
01:45:45,040 --> 01:45:47,879
There is nothing you can take from me, Osman.

1005
01:45:48,040 --> 01:45:51,079
I will never serve you.

1006
01:45:51,440 --> 01:45:55,759
Kill me here when you have a chance.

1007
01:45:55,880 --> 01:45:59,799
Or you will regret.

1008
01:46:09,360 --> 01:46:13,199
You helped us and you will again.

1009
01:46:13,560 --> 01:46:17,079
We'll enter Mekece thanks to you.

1010
01:46:20,760 --> 01:46:23,519
-Oghuz!
-My Bey.

1011
01:46:23,880 --> 01:46:27,079
Take this...

1012
01:46:30,000 --> 01:46:34,679
...and the ones behind him to the tribe.

1013
01:46:38,320 --> 01:46:41,119
Beat them well.

1014
01:46:42,000 --> 01:46:46,159
-Make them ready to speak to me.
-As you order, my Bey.

1015
01:46:51,000 --> 01:46:55,879
My Bey, give Ulcay to me. He
and I have an unfinished business.

1016
01:46:59,440 --> 01:47:01,999
Solgur Agha.

1017
01:47:02,760 --> 01:47:06,679
-Just be patient.
-As you order, my Bey.

1018
01:47:08,320 --> 01:47:11,199
-Come on.
-Take him, Oghuz.

1019
01:47:30,280 --> 01:47:32,479
Well, son..

1020
01:47:32,600 --> 01:47:35,679
It's time to make Mekece the land of Turks.

1021
01:47:35,800 --> 01:47:38,959
-If Allah permits, my Bey.
-Let's go.

1022
01:47:39,120 --> 01:47:40,839
Let's get on horses.

1023
01:47:42,480 --> 01:47:45,879
I have a question for you, Gunduz Bey.

1024
01:47:46,040 --> 01:47:50,239
Osman gave you everything you wanted.

1025
01:47:50,680 --> 01:47:55,119
But still, you wanted your daughter...

1026
01:47:55,480 --> 01:47:59,839
...to marry his son. Why?

1027
01:48:03,560 --> 01:48:06,159
For the same reason...

1028
01:48:06,440 --> 01:48:11,159
...why you wanted your daughter to marry...

1029
01:48:11,640 --> 01:48:15,799
...Ibrahim Bey's son. Now you answer.

1030
01:48:17,240 --> 01:48:21,559
Because I know the strength comes from unity.

1031
01:48:21,680 --> 01:48:25,159
Well... That's it.

1032
01:48:25,280 --> 01:48:30,799
If you choose our side

1033
01:48:31,160 --> 01:48:36,599
...we'll offer you greater strength, Gunduz Bey.

1034
01:48:40,560 --> 01:48:44,079
-I hear you. -Orhan...

1035
01:48:44,240 --> 01:48:47,199
...is your son-in-law.

1036
01:48:48,000 --> 01:48:53,039
If you take our side, our job will be easier.

1037
01:48:53,600 --> 01:48:56,359
Osman will have no power left to resist.

1038
01:48:56,360 --> 01:48:59,519
But if he still resists

1039
01:48:59,600 --> 01:49:04,279
...then Kayi will obey your orders.

1040
01:49:10,000 --> 01:49:15,799
What makes you really
think I'm going to accept this?

1041
01:49:17,360 --> 01:49:20,319
Don't you see...

1042
01:49:20,520 --> 01:49:23,919
...Osman is putting people in danger, Gunduz Bey?

1043
01:49:24,160 --> 01:49:29,199
He's declaring war against us.
Don't you see the consequences?

1044
01:49:30,720 --> 01:49:33,639
You have no chances to win...

1045
01:49:34,120 --> 01:49:37,399
...while Lords support us.

1046
01:49:39,000 --> 01:49:40,999
Gunduz Bey.

1047
01:49:41,000 --> 01:49:45,039
You should stand on our side.

1048
01:49:45,160 --> 01:49:50,759
So Kayi people will have a shadow
to stay under when the war begins.

1049
01:49:54,280 --> 01:49:57,079
We have no problems with Kayi.

1050
01:49:57,200 --> 01:50:01,999
We have a problem with Osman. Join us.

1051
01:50:02,720 --> 01:50:05,079
We can stop him together.

1052
01:50:05,360 --> 01:50:08,279
Protect your people from this war.

1053
01:50:08,760 --> 01:50:11,639
Reduce the brother's blood.

1054
01:50:16,760 --> 01:50:22,159
If it's inevitable, it's good to reduce.

1055
01:50:24,720 --> 01:50:27,199
What about the trade?

1056
01:50:28,640 --> 01:50:33,079
That's it, Gunduz Bey. Let's
speak the same language.

1057
01:50:33,800 --> 01:50:37,439
If you take our side

1058
01:50:37,680 --> 01:50:40,559
..we'll let you be a sharer.

1059
01:50:40,920 --> 01:50:45,839
A lion's share for the lion, Gunduz Bey.

1060
01:50:46,480 --> 01:50:51,479
-Don't be worrying.
-Thank you, thank you.

1061
01:50:52,480 --> 01:50:55,159
We're together then.

1062
01:50:55,280 --> 01:51:01,159
Let's leave to welcome our guests then.

1063
01:51:01,240 --> 01:51:03,959
-Let's go.
-Come on.

1064
01:51:04,240 --> 01:51:07,599
Who are the guests?

1065
01:51:33,640 --> 01:51:36,999
How did it happen, Husrev? Where did you catch him?

1066
01:51:38,200 --> 01:51:40,599
He had a grudge with Ulcay,

1067
01:51:40,880 --> 01:51:43,399
...attempted to raid the settlement...

1068
01:51:43,680 --> 01:51:45,839
...and fell into the jackal's trap.

1069
01:51:46,080 --> 01:51:51,239
What a strange world! Since when has the
wolf been falling into the jackal's trap?

1070
01:51:51,280 --> 01:51:55,359
Put Osman Bey in the dungeon. Beys
will deliver a judgement when they come.

1071
01:51:55,520 --> 01:51:59,799
As long as you seek vengeance

1072
01:52:01,280 --> 01:52:04,559
...you will always lose.

1073
01:52:08,320 --> 01:52:12,839
And you? Who is behind you?

1074
01:52:15,480 --> 01:52:18,719
Look into my eyes! Look!

1075
01:52:19,520 --> 01:52:23,759
Do I look like a man who
would leave a Turk's fate to you?

1076
01:52:30,480 --> 01:52:33,974
They're looking for a chance
to break you, Osman Bey.

1077
01:52:33,986 --> 01:52:35,479
Well... Not like you.

1078
01:52:37,360 --> 01:52:39,919
They're still our enemy.

1079
01:52:40,920 --> 01:52:44,159
We're not here to be captive...

1080
01:52:46,840 --> 01:52:50,759
...but to capture Mekece.

1081
01:52:57,800 --> 01:53:00,479
Orhan.

1082
01:53:01,360 --> 01:53:03,679
Alaaddin.

1083
01:53:06,600 --> 01:53:11,439
Don't. Don't you take
another step towards my father.

1084
01:53:11,600 --> 01:53:15,079
Archers, attack! Kill them all!

1085
01:53:18,200 --> 01:53:19,679
How could this happen?

1086
01:53:25,600 --> 01:53:28,279
It's time for a guard change.

1087
01:53:28,280 --> 01:53:34,839
Before Osman Bey arrives, we'll
climb up and put on their clothes.

1088
01:53:37,800 --> 01:53:39,799
My Bey!

1089
01:53:40,320 --> 01:53:45,159
What is it, Commander? You
already started stepping back.

1090
01:53:45,720 --> 01:53:48,359
Soldiers, attack!

1091
01:53:52,120 --> 01:53:54,768
We have never been
captives since the day we were

1092
01:53:54,780 --> 01:53:57,439
born. We will not be slaves
to anyone from now on!

1093
01:53:59,080 --> 01:54:04,439
Alps! Go everywhere! Don't let any of them survive!

1094
01:55:51,440 --> 01:55:57,679
Close the doors! protect
the castle! No one will get in!

1095
01:56:27,800 --> 01:56:31,719
While investigating, we encountered the monks.

1096
01:56:31,720 --> 01:56:34,164
We heard that the
person Melike Hatun killed

1097
01:56:34,176 --> 01:56:36,959
because she claimed he
was the killer of her son...

1098
01:56:37,040 --> 01:56:40,199
...was actually a convict
sentenced to death in Bursa.

1099
01:56:40,320 --> 01:56:44,519
He escaped just three days after the murder.

1100
01:56:44,600 --> 01:56:48,359
How is that possible?
-Why, my daughter?

1101
01:56:48,480 --> 01:56:52,639
He was going to die anyway.
They turned his death...

1102
01:56:52,800 --> 01:56:55,839
...into a cheap show for someone's benefit.

1103
01:56:56,920 --> 01:57:01,519
So, Ahmet Bey's killer is still out there.

1104
01:57:06,680 --> 01:57:08,759
Thanks to this information...

1105
01:57:09,080 --> 01:57:13,319
...you're preventing a major
war, Yunus Emre. Thank you.

1106
01:57:13,480 --> 01:57:17,439
There's more, Bala Hatun. The fake judge...

1107
01:57:17,600 --> 01:57:22,239
...was the judge in Kastamonu
during the Cobanogullari era.

1108
01:57:22,840 --> 01:57:26,759
He was dismissed from his position for...

1109
01:57:27,040 --> 01:57:30,039
...going against justice and engaging in haram.

1110
01:57:30,440 --> 01:57:32,559
Kastamonu?

1111
01:57:33,080 --> 01:57:36,759
Then Candaroglu must be involved.

1112
01:57:37,360 --> 01:57:41,839
Why would Candaroglu prevent them
from finding his own children's killer?

1113
01:57:41,920 --> 01:57:43,799
Because he has already made...

1114
01:57:43,880 --> 01:57:46,599
...his judgment in his own court.

1115
01:57:46,680 --> 01:57:49,479
He doesn't want his verdict to be proven wrong.

1116
01:57:49,760 --> 01:57:53,199
He wants justice to prevail...

1117
01:57:53,280 --> 01:57:57,799
...but it's his justice that he seeks.

1118
01:57:57,960 --> 01:58:03,559
His arrogance is so great
that it magnifies his pain.

1119
01:58:03,840 --> 01:58:07,559
And that pain makes him
think that he has the right to...

1120
01:58:07,560 --> 01:58:10,199
...do everything.

1121
01:58:10,360 --> 01:58:13,319
Especially when it's a...

1122
01:58:13,600 --> 01:58:18,159
...grieving mother accusing
someone as her son's murder...

1123
01:58:20,160 --> 01:58:23,879
Ah, Melike Hatun, ah...

1124
01:58:27,760 --> 01:58:30,959
May it be good.

1125
01:58:33,400 --> 01:58:38,919
Alps are coming!
Alps are coming!

1126
01:58:40,280 --> 01:58:44,039
Boran Bey and Konur Bey are captives!

1127
01:58:44,880 --> 01:58:49,159
Bala Hatun! The captives are coming!

1128
01:58:49,600 --> 01:58:52,799
Boran Bey and Konur Bey are coming!

1129
01:58:57,040 --> 01:58:59,879
Take your last breaths, Gonca.

1130
01:58:59,960 --> 01:59:03,759
I will send you to hell.

1131
01:59:12,720 --> 01:59:16,959
Olcay... He got caught.

1132
01:59:21,520 --> 01:59:23,719
He will never speak.

1133
01:59:44,200 --> 01:59:47,439
These three of them are
now our captives, Bala Hatun.

1134
01:59:50,560 --> 01:59:53,279
Stop!

1135
01:59:55,280 --> 01:59:57,359
While these men were in our service..

1136
01:59:57,520 --> 02:00:01,359
-...how can you...
Don't you say something, Melike Hatun.

1137
02:00:01,560 --> 02:00:05,839
Stay out of this.

1138
02:00:11,160 --> 02:00:15,159
Oghuz Alp. Take these dogs to the square.

1139
02:00:15,280 --> 02:00:16,719
Tie them up.

1140
02:00:16,920 --> 02:00:20,159
Start questioning them.
-Yes, Bala Hatun.

1141
02:00:20,320 --> 02:00:23,079
Walk! -Traitors!

1142
02:00:35,560 --> 02:00:40,759
That Olcay dog was involved in your son's death.

1143
02:00:43,480 --> 02:00:46,439
We just want justice, Melike Hatun.

1144
02:00:46,800 --> 02:00:48,639
So that you came here for peace...

1145
02:00:48,920 --> 02:00:51,879
...you should know that
we are doing this for peace.

1146
02:00:52,040 --> 02:00:54,719
Or else... you can leave.

1147
02:01:54,840 --> 02:01:57,879
Come on, Alps! We are going there!

1148
02:02:10,920 --> 02:02:13,799
Hang on, brothers! Hang on!

1149
02:02:32,320 --> 02:02:36,439
Step back, Osman Bey. Don't make
me do things that I don't want to do.

1150
02:02:36,800 --> 02:02:39,479
You are quite impulsive.

1151
02:02:39,560 --> 02:02:43,799
You will die and it will be a pity.
-Listen to him, Tugay.

1152
02:02:43,880 --> 02:02:47,159
Drop your sword.
-My duty is to protect the castle!

1153
02:02:47,280 --> 02:02:51,679
It is the order of my Bey. If I
need to die, I will die for sure.

1154
02:02:51,840 --> 02:02:54,879
But I will not give the castle to you, Osman Bey.

1155
02:03:01,760 --> 02:03:06,159
Even though you stayed
with your father Ibrahim Bey...

1156
02:03:06,320 --> 02:03:08,519
...you still have a bit of..

1157
02:03:08,640 --> 02:03:12,759
...morals and conscience in you.

1158
02:03:13,360 --> 02:03:17,599
I do as my Bey says. But if a Turk Bey...

1159
02:03:17,680 --> 02:03:24,319
...ever faces the sword of infidels
I never step back, Osman Bey.

1160
02:03:48,080 --> 02:03:50,879
Don't fight for no reason. The castle has fallen.

1161
02:03:51,000 --> 02:03:54,439
Surrender, so you can survive, Alps.

1162
02:03:55,040 --> 02:03:58,119
Drop your swords.

1163
02:04:01,240 --> 02:04:04,359
Calm down, brother.

1164
02:04:27,840 --> 02:04:31,919
May your new castle be blessed,
Osman Bey! The castle has fallen!

1165
02:04:32,080 --> 02:04:34,599
Victory is ours with Allah's permission!

1166
02:04:34,680 --> 02:04:36,039
Allah is the Greatest!

1167
02:04:36,360 --> 02:04:43,799
-Allah is the Greatest!
-Allah is the Greatest!

1168
02:04:44,240 --> 02:04:46,439
Thank you, thank you.
Long live.

1169
02:04:46,800 --> 02:04:49,759
But the property only belongs to Allah.

1170
02:04:49,920 --> 02:04:55,319
We are just protecting the trust.

1171
02:04:56,320 --> 02:04:59,319
Come here.

1172
02:05:06,320 --> 02:05:09,879
Take him to the dungeon.

1173
02:05:10,200 --> 02:05:14,719
Let him think about who should he support.

1174
02:05:31,680 --> 02:05:36,519
-Where are you going?
-I'll put our banner where it belongs.

1175
02:05:36,880 --> 02:05:38,319
Alright, alright.

1176
02:05:38,400 --> 02:05:42,119
But stop, wait. Let the Beys come.

1177
02:05:42,440 --> 02:05:46,919
-If Allah permits, we will put it after that.
-Yes, my Bey.

1178
02:06:23,520 --> 02:06:27,559
I bring you greetings from holy Rome.

1179
02:06:28,280 --> 02:06:31,119
Thank you, Commander.

1180
02:06:31,320 --> 02:06:35,119
We brought you the glorious Bey of Kayi

1181
02:06:35,280 --> 02:06:38,559
Gunduz Bey.

1182
02:06:41,760 --> 02:06:44,639
He is Orhan's father-in-law.

1183
02:06:44,880 --> 02:06:49,039
He's a glorious fighter.

1184
02:06:49,320 --> 02:06:54,479
Great. Then we have many
things to talk about, Beys.

1185
02:06:54,760 --> 02:07:00,239
-Let's go to the castle.
-Come on.

1186
02:07:20,080 --> 02:07:23,239
We need to get out of here
before Osman Bey arrives.

1187
02:07:23,360 --> 02:07:26,439
This tribe was once your tribe, Boran.

1188
02:07:27,160 --> 02:07:30,039
Why are you in a hurry?

1189
02:07:30,280 --> 02:07:33,519
Look how frightened they look.

1190
02:07:33,800 --> 02:07:39,239
When we get out of here,
they will drown in their blood.

1191
02:07:41,800 --> 02:07:47,399
I know Osman very well. He didn't just capture us.

1192
02:07:47,600 --> 02:07:50,632
He captured Ibrahim
Bey and Yakup Bey as well.

1193
02:07:50,644 --> 02:07:52,039
If you know him well,

1194
02:07:52,560 --> 02:07:55,959
tell me. What does he want?

1195
02:07:56,080 --> 02:07:59,479
He's trying to pin Shahzade Ahmed's death on us.

1196
02:08:01,000 --> 02:08:04,999
That Byzantine killed Ahmed
everyone can witness to it.

1197
02:08:05,120 --> 02:08:08,039
But we don't know who's he serving to, Konur.

1198
02:08:08,600 --> 02:08:11,879
Osman will find a fake evidence
and make everyone believe.

1199
02:08:12,080 --> 02:08:13,919
You're right.

1200
02:08:14,000 --> 02:08:17,399
It's clear where they will find those evidence.

1201
02:08:18,520 --> 02:08:23,159
-Rukneddin The Judge death is a mystery.
-That's right.

1202
02:08:23,920 --> 02:08:27,177
Is it possible for Byzantines
to kill a judge in these lands?

1203
02:08:27,189 --> 02:08:28,279
Enough!

1204
02:08:30,000 --> 02:08:32,439
You've bothered me.

1205
02:08:32,800 --> 02:08:38,559
It is possible to kill without making it obvious.

1206
02:08:39,480 --> 02:08:42,439
I can see it now.

1207
02:08:42,520 --> 02:08:46,359
How did Orhan find Rukneddin The Judge?

1208
02:08:47,400 --> 02:08:52,359
What if the murderer serves Osman?

1209
02:09:07,840 --> 02:09:10,439
He knew about what we did.

1210
02:09:10,520 --> 02:09:14,559
Brother, this dastard knew about everything.

1211
02:09:18,840 --> 02:09:23,279
Kill them, traitors!

1212
02:09:30,480 --> 02:09:34,839
When the blood feud of Shahzade Ahmed is over

1213
02:09:34,920 --> 02:09:39,799
Kayis women sheathed their swords.

1214
02:09:39,880 --> 02:09:42,399
Women.

1215
02:09:42,480 --> 02:09:44,439
When the swords are unsheathed

1216
02:09:44,680 --> 02:09:48,759
they won't be sheathed until
they cut your head, dastard.

1217
02:09:48,960 --> 02:09:52,319
But first, you'll talk.

1218
02:09:52,400 --> 02:09:55,919
Everyone will find out the evil things he did.

1219
02:09:56,240 --> 02:09:58,559
Mouthy woman.

1220
02:09:58,720 --> 02:10:03,639
I didn't do anything without
Ibrahim Bey's knowledge.

1221
02:10:04,320 --> 02:10:07,199
Isn't that right, Melike Hatun?

1222
02:10:10,680 --> 02:10:14,999
They'd say one would change. I know you,

1223
02:10:15,080 --> 02:10:18,399
but if you played any
tricks, they will be revealed.

1224
02:10:19,000 --> 02:10:23,599
-Ulcay.
-Don't trust these witches.

1225
02:10:23,880 --> 02:10:26,799
They're not the murderers of their child

1226
02:10:26,920 --> 02:10:31,359
-but they're as guilty as the murderer.
-Enough!

1227
02:10:31,440 --> 02:10:35,159
You can't spit your poison anymore.

1228
02:10:38,680 --> 02:10:41,039
Oguz Alp.

1229
02:10:52,520 --> 02:10:56,919
Even if you strip my flesh from my bones

1230
02:10:57,520 --> 02:11:00,799
you won't be able to wash this blood off you.

1231
02:11:00,960 --> 02:11:04,319
Don't waste your breath in vain.

1232
02:11:05,240 --> 02:11:08,279
You'll talk when Osman Bey comes anyway.

1233
02:11:08,400 --> 02:11:11,879
Either gladly or with torture.

1234
02:11:12,160 --> 02:11:16,239
But the truth will be revealed.

1235
02:12:41,120 --> 02:12:44,799
Osman.

1236
02:13:32,840 --> 02:13:36,879
Gunduz Bey. Did you welcome the Beys well?

1237
02:13:37,480 --> 02:13:39,519
As you requested,

1238
02:13:39,680 --> 02:13:42,279
we welcomed them very well, Osman Bey.

1239
02:13:42,400 --> 02:13:45,279
We didn't offend anyone...

1240
02:13:45,520 --> 02:13:48,639
...and we had a great conversation.

1241
02:13:48,760 --> 02:13:53,439
Alright, alright. You did well.

1242
02:13:53,760 --> 02:13:58,159
Now I'll welcome them in my property Mekece.

1243
02:14:00,720 --> 02:14:06,079
We'll sit altogether and we'll
talk about the evil alliance.

1244
02:14:08,800 --> 02:14:12,479
We will all see whose head will...

1245
02:14:12,800 --> 02:14:14,879
...remain on his body...

1246
02:14:14,960 --> 02:14:16,799
...and whose will fall.

1247
02:14:25,255 --> 02:14:36,545
Visit turkision.com for more!